From 85b6a87031a03493cec10a8116aa447ed2d98dd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:21:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 74/75] hw/display/pvg: on-disk shader caches, presents on the
 executor thread

Translations (SPIR-V per SHA-256 of the translator inputs) and the
VkPipelineCache are kept under $XDG_CACHE_HOME/pvg, keyed by the QEMU
binary; caches of other builds go after a week. PVG_NO_DISK_CACHE=1
disables them.

With the async worker, Transaction3 no longer drains the worker under
the BQL and copies the frame on the vCPU: it is queued behind the
command buffers it shows. The worker reads the frame and records the
rows that changed; a bottom half copies only those (applying gamma),
updates that band of the console and signals the present. Mission
Control test: 16.1-16.8 -> 17.0-17.6 presents/s.

PVG_DIAG_REDUNDANT=1 logs how many uploaded bytes repeat the previous
upload of the same range (measurement only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
